# What does not go to the deployment.
#
# roster.html DOES go, by the owner's decision on 25 Sep 2026. It is served at
# /roster.html and nothing in index.html links to it, so it is a link you send
# rather than a page anyone lands on from the board.
#
# Two guards ride with it and each is one line to reverse:
#
#   - SHOW_CURRENT in the page is false, so anybody still enrolled shows as
#     "Jayden A." rather than by name. Alumni are named.
#   - the page carries <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow">, so the
#     link works when you send it without 749 named teenagers' career pages
#     entering a search index. Publishing a link and publishing to search are
#     different decisions and only the first has been made.
#
# No vercel.json change was needed. roster.html sits at the root, so it matches
# the /((?!pull).*) rule and takes the app's own CSP: default-src none, fonts
# from gstatic, connect-src none. The page makes no requests of its own - three
# external references, all Google Fonts, and zero fetches.
#
# The raw archive stays out. The page embeds everything it needs, so serving
# the CSVs as well would widen what is public without making anything work.
# They remain in the repo, which is where the tests read them from.
pull/roster/
